	"metadata": {
		"note": "Six rooms in a line, one sigil in each. threshold: a vertical fold, and riding the unfold up. span: a pit closed with one hand and a socket, then taken apart from the far side. cistern: water you can climb and cannot pin in. press: weight plates, three hands, and which goes where. annex: a sealed chamber entered through the inside of a fold. vault: the same idea turned on its side, with one hand, because the other is on the keystone back in the annex. What each room is for is in scripts/world/README.md; scripts/tests/test_overworld_solutions.gd plays every one and is the authority on whether they can be done."
	},
